users/prwhelan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description\n\nFrom: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/107251\r\n\r\nWhile a cluster is upgrading, we see `IndexNotFoundException` for some Transforms.\r\nExample:\r\n```java\r\n[endpoint.metadata_united-default-8.13.0] transform has failed; experienced: [Failed to index documents into destination index due to permanent error: [org.elasticsearch.xpack.transform.transforms.BulkIndexingException: Bulk index experienced [36] failures and at least 1 irrecoverable [org.elasticsearch.index.IndexNotFoundException: no such index [.metrics-endpoint.metadata_united_default]]. Other failures: [RemoteTransportException] message [org.elasticsearch.transport.RemoteTransportException: [<>][<>][indices:data/write/bulk[s]]]; org.elasticsearch.index.IndexNotFoundException: no such index [.metrics-endpoint.metadata_united_default]]].\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is likely an eventual consistency issue, and the transform needs to give the index time to become consistently reachable","closed_by":{"login":"prwhelan","id":1223797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjM3OTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1223797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan","html_url":"https://github.com/prwhelan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/followers","following_